@@ -88,9 +88,9 @@ URL opening, webpage conversion, and Word conversion require the desktop app. Fa
 
 ### Edit existing text and images
 
-Choose **Edit mode**, then click the text you want to change and type on the page. Press **Enter** or click outside the line to apply it. **Esc** cancels typing. Clear a line to delete it.
+Choose **Edit mode**, then click the text you want to change. The cursor starts at the end of the line. **Backspace** deletes the previous character and **Delete** deletes the next one. Press **Enter** or click outside the line to apply it. **Esc** cancels typing. Clear the line and press Enter, or choose **Remove line**, to delete those words from the PDF. That removes the text objects. It does not cover them with a box.
 
-Click an embedded picture and choose **Replace image…** to select a PNG or JPEG. You can leave Edit mode to read your changes or use **Save copy** to export and open the edited PDF.
+Click an embedded picture and choose **Replace image…** to select a PNG or JPEG, or **Remove image** to delete that placement. Backspace or Delete also removes the selected picture when you are not typing in a text field. Escape or a click away dismisses the controls. You can leave Edit mode to read your changes or use **Save copy** to export and open the edited PDF. Removing a placement does not paint over the picture, and it is not a secure redaction: an unused image stream can remain in the file. Signature marks made with the Sign tool are annotations, not this picture control.
 
 Open **More → Version history** to review your changes. Saving a changed copy keeps the original PDF and a numbered version on this device. Text edits show the old and new wording, and image replacements show the filename and page. Open or download an earlier version from the panel. History is available for unencrypted PDFs up to 50 MB and can be cleared per document.
 
